// Rule: T4-LOLBAS-Sysinternals-privileged-context-isolate   [STAGING]
//
// Highest-tier, high-confidence malicious activity that runs in privileged /
// admin / SYSTEM context — credential theft, destructive impact, lateral
// movement. Spans LOLBAS binaries, Sysinternals(-adjacent) tools, and DC
// tooling — the cross-family "critical -> auto-isolate" bucket above the
// T1-T3 LOLBAS tiers.
//
// SCOPE = "does not EXCLUDE privileged accounts" (interpretation #1), NOT
// "only privileged accounts". These techniques must be caught in ANY context —
// scoping to admin-only would blind non-admin/service-account cases that T1-T3
// don't cover. The rule simply drops the admin/SYSTEM exclusion that T1-T3 use,
// via the MINIMAL header below. (If you want admin-ONLY, invert to a positive
// InitiatingProcessAccountName filter instead — see note.)
//
// Response tier: isolate. Keep in STAGING until volume is understood, then
// dedupe against T3 / the Sysinternals rule (see overlap notes at bottom).
// Shared exclusions via the saved function FilteredProcessEvents (see
// shared-functions.kql). excludeAdmin = FALSE = MINIMAL: NO account exclusion,
// because these techniques run in admin/SYSTEM context by design. Do not
// "helpfully" flip it to true. (For an admin-ONLY variant, add a positive
// `| where InitiatingProcessAccountName has_any ("adm_", "administrator", ...)` after the call.)
FilteredProcessEvents(false)   // excludeAdmin = false (MINIMAL — keeps every account)
| where
    (1 == 2)   // inert seed — every detection below starts with `or`, so any line toggles freely
    // --- Credential access ---
    // NOTE: procdump + psexec below are SYSINTERNALS tools, also covered by the separate
    // Sysinternals rule. That rule excludes admin/SYSTEM (generic-usage noise); this rule keeps
    // them WITHOUT the exclusion on purpose — these weaponized argument patterns run elevated by
    // design, so this is the safety net for exactly the context the Sysinternals rule drops.
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "procdump.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("-ma", "lsass"))            // T1003.001 LSASS dump [Sysinternals]
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "rundll32.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "comsvcs.dll" and ProcessCommandLine has "MiniDump")  // T1003.001 LSASS via comsvcs
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "reg.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "save" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("sam", "security", "system"))  // T1003.002 hive dump
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "esentutl.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("/y", "/vss") and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("ntds", ".dit", "sam"))  // T1003.003 NTDS/SAM copy
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "ntdsutil.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("ifm", "create full"))       // T1003.003 NTDS.dit extraction (DC)
    // --- Impact / anti-recovery ---
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "vssadmin.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "delete" and ProcessCommandLine has "shadows")  // T1490 shadow-copy deletion
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "wbadmin.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "delete" and ProcessCommandLine has_any ("catalog", "backup", "systemstatebackup"))  // T1490 backup deletion
    // --- Defense evasion / anti-forensics (often SYSTEM) ---
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "wevtutil.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "cl")                             // T1070.001 clear event log [sole owner — removed from T3]
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "fsutil.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "usn" and ProcessCommandLine has "deletejournal")  // T1070 USN journal wipe
    // --- Lateral movement ---
    or (ProcessCommandLine has_any ("psexec.exe", "psexec64.exe", "paexec.exe"))                           // T1569.002 / T1021.002 service exec [Sysinternals/clone]
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "winrs.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "-r:")                               // T1021.006 remote shell
    or (ProcessCommandLine has "wmic.exe" and ProcessCommandLine has "/node:" and ProcessCommandLine has_all ("process", "call", "create"))  // T1047 remote WMI exec
| extend Severity = "Critical"
| order by Timestamp desc

// --- OVERLAP NOTES (resolve before graduating from staging) ---
// 1. wevtutil cl ownership — RESOLVED (2026-07 dedup): removed from T3, this T4 rule is the
//    sole owner. Rationale: log-clear runs in SYSTEM/admin context that the T3 GLOBAL header
//    excludes, so the no-account-exclusion T4 header is the correct scope, and it already
//    covered the non-admin case too — so removing the T3 line lost no coverage. (It remains a
//    constituent of the behaviour burst rules by design — chains reuse owned commands.)
// 2. procdump + psexec are also in the separate Sysinternals rule, which excludes admin.
//    Intended division: Sysinternals rule = generic/user-context usage; this rule = the
//    weaponized argument patterns in admin/SYSTEM context the Sysinternals rule drops.
//    (Note: procdump is caught by that rule's ProductName="Sysinternals" clause even though
//    it's not in its explicit FileName list — so non-admin procdump is already covered there.)
